We can solve this system of equations using the method of elimination.
Multiplying the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 5, we get \begin{align*}
6x-10y&=-22,\\
35x+10y&=-60.
\end{align*}
Adding the two equations, we eliminate the variable $y$ and get \begin{align*}
6x-10y+35x+10y&=-22-60,\\
41x&=-82,
\end{align*}which gives us $x=-2.$
Substituting this value back into the first equation, we have \begin{align*}
3(-2)-5y&=-11,\\
-6-5y&=-11,\\
-5y&=-5,\\
y&=1.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the solution to the system of equations is $(x,y)=\boxed{(-2,1)}$.The answer is: (-2,1)

